WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.840
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:05.110 --> 00:06.111
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION.

3
00:06.194 --> 00:08.030
THERE IS NO RELATION TO REAL PEOPLE OR EVENTS.

4
00:12.618 --> 00:14.036
[panting]

5
00:16.288 --> 00:17.372
[in Korean] Wait.

6
00:18.415 --> 00:23.378
Karin, wait. Please, hear me out.

7
00:23.462 --> 00:27.549
[panting] About earlier…

8
00:28.050 --> 00:29.968
I don't want you to misunderstand.

9
00:33.680 --> 00:35.182
[in English] You came for this land?

10
00:36.183 --> 00:37.184
Ah…

11
00:37.809 --> 00:40.395
The land? Ah, the land.

12
00:41.730 --> 00:44.900
[sighs, speaks Korean] It's true.

13
00:44.983 --> 00:47.069
At first, I came here because I wanted the land.

14
00:47.152 --> 00:49.863
Okay, so I… Ah, um, wait. Hold on.

15
00:51.490 --> 00:53.533
This land… Wait.

16
00:54.117 --> 00:57.120
Please, hear me out.

17
00:57.204 --> 01:02.793
I meant to explain all this to you…

18
01:02.876 --> 01:05.337
[device beeping]

19
01:05.420 --> 01:07.005
[breathing heavily]

20
01:08.006 --> 01:09.216
-[Karin gasps] -You okay?

21
01:24.606 --> 01:25.816
[in English] Please…

22
01:28.902 --> 01:30.112
I need you to leave.

23
01:31.488 --> 01:32.739
Get out of my house…

24
01:34.574 --> 01:35.784
and get off my land.

25
01:41.998 --> 01:43.083
I thank you…

26
01:45.710 --> 01:47.170
for everything.

27
02:13.071 --> 02:15.741
EPISODE 6

28
02:16.241 --> 02:18.952
[♪ sorrowful music playing]

29
02:42.309 --> 02:45.520
[stammers] Have either of you seen Karin lately?

30
02:46.104 --> 02:47.564
It's been a while…

31
02:47.647 --> 02:51.735
Well, here's an idea. Why don't we pay her a visit soon?

32
02:51.818 --> 02:53.862
-[villager 1] Yeah… -[villager 2] Sure…

33
02:56.573 --> 02:58.575
-Oh! [chuckles] -[chuckles]

34
02:58.658 --> 03:00.076
Here's Karin!

35
03:00.160 --> 03:03.622
-Oh, you're a sight for sore eyes. -Hello! It's been ages, Karin.

36
03:03.705 --> 03:05.123
Good to see you.

37
03:05.207 --> 03:07.125
Things have been busy lately, sorry.

38
03:07.209 --> 03:09.461
-[chuckles] -Don't run yourself into the ground.

39
03:10.086 --> 03:11.087
I won't.

40
03:11.171 --> 03:12.172
I'll see you later.

41
03:14.549 --> 03:16.092
[villager 1] Bye.

42
03:16.968 --> 03:17.969
[sighs]

43
03:29.189 --> 03:30.690
[♪ sad piano music playing]

44
03:39.908 --> 03:41.576
All right. [sniffs]

45
03:42.619 --> 03:44.621
Back to doing what I do best.

46
03:46.206 --> 03:47.207
[chuckles]

47
03:47.958 --> 03:48.959
[sighs]

48
03:54.714 --> 03:56.216
Okay…

49
04:11.690 --> 04:13.608
[pen scribbling]

50
04:21.908 --> 04:23.285
[in Korean] You're early.

51
04:24.786 --> 04:26.079
How are you adjusting?

52
04:27.122 --> 04:28.582
It's been a while since you last worked on site.

53
04:28.665 --> 04:33.128
This is what I used to do.

54
04:34.004 --> 04:35.088
[scoffs]

55
04:35.171 --> 04:36.882
Ever the workaholic.

56
04:37.883 --> 04:39.342
Let's grab lunch later.

57
04:40.760 --> 04:41.803
[sighs]

58
04:42.387 --> 04:43.847
[footsteps depart]

59
04:51.354 --> 04:52.355
[sighs]

60
04:53.607 --> 04:55.775
[♪ pensive music playing]

61
05:08.705 --> 05:09.706
[phone buzzes]

62
05:13.960 --> 05:15.962
CHIEF - KARIN, PLEASE SUBMIT THE DOCUMENTS I ASKED FOR

63
05:16.046 --> 05:17.047
BY NOON TOMORROW.

64
06:04.427 --> 06:05.470
[in Korean] It's nice.

65
06:17.983 --> 06:21.152
[in English] Kunam, you seen Mari around?

66
06:22.570 --> 06:25.615
I stopped by Serendipity but it looks like they're closed.

67
06:25.699 --> 06:27.993
No. Have you given her a call?

68
06:28.076 --> 06:29.661
Oh, uh…

69
06:29.744 --> 06:31.955
You know what, I have, and she's not answering.

70
06:33.748 --> 06:36.292
Same for you, right? You haven't heard from her either?

71
06:37.919 --> 06:39.546
-Right. -Hmm.

72
06:40.213 --> 06:41.589
Wonder if she's okay…

73
06:42.549 --> 06:43.842
This is weird.

74
06:46.052 --> 06:49.472
-Well, I should get going. -Sure. Have a good one.

75
06:49.556 --> 06:50.724
Yep.

76
07:04.529 --> 07:06.656
[in Korean] We restructured the layout.

77
07:06.740 --> 07:08.533
As for the first floor…

78
07:08.616 --> 07:11.202
-Let's adjust this layout a little… -Yes, sir.

79
07:11.286 --> 07:12.871
[coworker] Sir, could you have a look at these too?

80
07:12.954 --> 07:15.248
We're thinking either Urban Latte or Urban Khaki…

81
07:16.082 --> 07:17.083
Hmm.

82
07:17.917 --> 07:19.419
What material will this be made out of?

83
07:19.502 --> 07:23.715
I'll have them ready by tomorrow morning and report back to you.

84
07:23.798 --> 07:25.049
Good work.

85
07:25.133 --> 07:26.551
[employees] Good work.

86
07:46.488 --> 07:47.614
[sighs]

87
07:49.616 --> 07:51.367
[phone buzzing]

88
07:54.245 --> 07:55.330
[sighs]

89
08:01.711 --> 08:02.712
Hey.

90
08:03.630 --> 08:05.965
I know you guys are busy. Why'd you come all the way down here?

91
08:06.049 --> 08:09.552
Can't exactly chitchat…

92
08:09.636 --> 08:11.554
-[Yubin groans] -…unless I come see you.

93
08:11.638 --> 08:15.558
[Sanggi] Plus, I bet you've been skipping your meals to keep working.

94
08:15.642 --> 08:18.603
Brought you food. Eat up.

95
08:18.686 --> 08:21.356
I appreciate it. This looks delicious.

96
08:21.439 --> 08:23.942
[phone buzzing]

97
08:29.113 --> 08:32.617
-What is it? Huh? -Sorry, I'm getting a call.

98
08:32.700 --> 08:34.410
-Go ahead and eat. -Oh…

99
08:34.494 --> 08:35.495
I see.

100
08:36.871 --> 08:38.540
He seems busy.

101
08:38.623 --> 08:43.253
[sighs] It's good to see Yubin back at work,

102
08:43.962 --> 08:48.716
but how did he end up working for Sia's company?

103
08:49.300 --> 08:51.761
They're like oil and water.

104
08:51.845 --> 08:54.430
He's got his reasons.

105
08:54.514 --> 08:55.515
And?

106
08:56.182 --> 08:57.809
Did you not know about this?

107
08:58.935 --> 09:01.771
Sia is already negotiating with the landowners around it.

108
09:02.355 --> 09:05.733
[sighs] Everyone's on board with the redevelopment,

109
09:06.276 --> 09:08.653
and they're collecting investments.

110
09:08.736 --> 09:10.947
He gets his career back, and he sells off his land.

111
09:11.030 --> 09:13.449
It's like killing two birds with one stone.

112
09:14.534 --> 09:17.078
-What? -Yubin set a condition.

113
09:17.162 --> 09:18.163
What is it?

114
09:18.997 --> 09:20.832
Yubin agreed to work at Bella Terra

115
09:20.915 --> 09:22.792
in exchange for them leaving that land alone.

116
09:24.711 --> 09:28.923
[sighs] Why does he care so much about Charo Island?

117
09:29.007 --> 09:30.175
Beats me.

118
09:32.135 --> 09:33.136
[grunts]

119
09:38.892 --> 09:39.893
[grunts]

120
09:57.493 --> 09:58.494
[in English] Huh?

121
09:59.579 --> 10:00.622
When did that…

122
10:21.601 --> 10:26.147
[in Korean] How many times did someone bump into this for it to look like this?

123
10:29.651 --> 10:30.860
[grunts]

124
10:41.120 --> 10:42.580
And to finish…

125
10:46.960 --> 10:48.086
Stars.

126
10:53.132 --> 10:54.384
Good.

127
11:14.988 --> 11:16.823
[♪ sad piano music playing]

128
11:21.411 --> 11:22.954
[can opening]

129
11:23.788 --> 11:26.499
[in English] Whoo, it's been so long!

130
11:26.582 --> 11:27.709
[in Korean] All right.

131
11:27.792 --> 11:29.711
-Cheers. -Cheers. [chuckles]

132
11:52.233 --> 11:53.234
[sighs]

133
12:03.411 --> 12:04.996
[Karin, in English] I'll trust you, Yubin.

134
12:10.209 --> 12:11.210
[sighs]

135
13:09.018 --> 13:10.686
[♪ music fades out]

136
13:35.795 --> 13:38.131
-[engine stops] -[car door opens, closes]

137
13:46.931 --> 13:48.724
Hi, Mr. Kurokawa.

138
13:50.393 --> 13:51.394
Hi, Karin.

139
13:56.816 --> 13:58.317
[rings]

140
14:08.953 --> 14:10.580
This place hasn't changed one bit.

141
14:11.080 --> 14:12.540
Is that where you do your research?

142
14:12.623 --> 14:13.833
It is.

143
14:13.916 --> 14:18.713
I do some there… And then also, I work in the greenhouse outside.

144
14:18.796 --> 14:20.006
-[grunts] -For the most part,

145
14:20.089 --> 14:22.967
I'm still using the tools my grandfather used before me.

146
14:24.177 --> 14:26.804
Good, good. So you won the Festa.

147
14:26.888 --> 14:29.724
I'm sorry I'm late, but congratulations.

148
14:31.267 --> 14:32.268
You truly deserve it.

149
14:33.644 --> 14:35.021
Thank you very much.

150
14:37.148 --> 14:39.442
To what do I owe the pleasure, Mr. Kurokawa?

151
14:41.819 --> 14:43.946
Well, in looking over some documents,

152
14:44.530 --> 14:46.574
I noticed that today is your birthday, isn't it?

153
14:46.657 --> 14:48.034
-Oh… -[chuckles]

154
14:48.117 --> 14:51.454
And there's one more reason to be celebrating.

155
14:51.996 --> 14:54.457
I thought this would be a great birthday present for you.

156
14:56.667 --> 14:59.253
PROOF OF CERTIFICATION

157
15:00.838 --> 15:04.050
You've officially been selected for Green Nova's mentorship.

158
15:04.884 --> 15:05.927
Congratulations.

159
15:09.305 --> 15:10.389
I was selected?

160
15:12.141 --> 15:14.727
But I thought they still had to do a field inspection.

161
15:14.810 --> 15:17.772
It's not necessary. You were the obvious pick.

162
15:18.689 --> 15:22.193
Your strawberries really were quite memorable, you know.

163
15:23.819 --> 15:26.447
Then, getting judged at the Festa was…

164
15:26.530 --> 15:28.866
That's right, that was the evaluation.

165
15:30.660 --> 15:33.204
I have a copy of your score sheet with me, right here.

166
15:37.875 --> 15:41.462
Karin, you've done great work up to now so keep it up.

167
15:44.715 --> 15:46.592
This means a lot to me. Thank you.

168
15:47.176 --> 15:48.386
Oh, please.

169
15:49.345 --> 15:50.596
This was your doing.

170
15:58.479 --> 16:00.398
[♪ pensive music playing]

171
16:04.735 --> 16:06.654
[Karin's grandfather] A city slicker like you must see this

172
16:06.737 --> 16:08.614
and think we live out in the sticks, huh?

173
16:08.698 --> 16:10.449
[chuckles] No, not at all.

174
16:10.533 --> 16:12.868
And thank you for letting me stay here with you.

175
16:13.536 --> 16:16.831
-This place is actually just my speed. -Oh.

176
16:16.914 --> 16:18.666
Why wouldn't you take your work to a lab?

177
16:19.750 --> 16:23.170
Well, the conditions are perfect here and that's hard to find.

178
16:23.254 --> 16:25.214
Soil quality, the sunlight…

179
16:25.298 --> 16:27.675
They're pretty hard to recreate indoors.

180
16:31.512 --> 16:35.141
Karin! Young lady, this farm is not your playground.

181
16:35.224 --> 16:38.144
I'm playing with the strawberries, Grandfather.

182
16:38.227 --> 16:41.522
And if you trample one of the seedlings, what'll you do then?

183
16:41.605 --> 16:43.607
There'll be less plants to play with.

184
16:45.276 --> 16:47.153
She's got a good head on her shoulders.

185
16:47.820 --> 16:51.240
Even running around the field like she is, she's avoiding the plants.

186
16:51.782 --> 16:53.826
It's like she's playing with the strawberries.

187
16:54.327 --> 16:55.870
[both chuckling]

188
17:01.625 --> 17:03.961
[Gyeongsu] She'll take over this place one day, won't she?

189
17:04.962 --> 17:07.882
Yes, I do think it's the right thing to do.

190
17:07.965 --> 17:09.050
-Hmm. -Uh-huh.

191
17:12.720 --> 17:14.889
[both chuckling]

192
17:33.115 --> 17:34.241
[grunts]

193
17:35.242 --> 17:36.619
Thank you, mister.

194
17:38.204 --> 17:39.580
You're Karin, right?

195
17:45.044 --> 17:46.295
I'll see you again, Karin.

196
17:51.801 --> 17:52.885
I'll see you again, Karin.

197
17:53.469 --> 17:54.470
Please.

198
17:56.889 --> 17:58.099
Ah, that's right.

199
18:00.017 --> 18:02.436
What do you think about creating a brand for your strawberries?

200
18:03.938 --> 18:05.398
Creating a brand, sir?

201
18:06.399 --> 18:08.109
-Then doesn't that mean… -Yes.

202
18:08.192 --> 18:10.069
Nationwide distribution.

203
18:10.152 --> 18:12.196
We could send your berries throughout Japan.

204
18:14.240 --> 18:17.827
Don't you want more people to experience your produce?

205
18:20.121 --> 18:21.580
Thank you for your faith in me.

206
18:22.331 --> 18:25.960
Uh… Although, I haven't perfected them yet.

207
18:26.043 --> 18:28.838
They are good enough as far as I'm concerned, Karin.

208
18:31.257 --> 18:33.676
Think it over and let me know.

209
18:34.969 --> 18:36.637
-I will. -All right.

210
19:10.629 --> 19:14.300
THE STRAWBERRIES WERE SET APART FROM THE GREENHOUSE PRODUCTS

211
19:24.685 --> 19:26.771
THE VISITORS FLOCKED TO THE BOOTH

212
19:26.854 --> 19:29.648
DURING THE FESTA'S BOOTH EXHIBITION

213
19:34.570 --> 19:37.573
WINNER INTERVIEW

214
19:41.702 --> 19:42.870
[door opens]

215
19:43.579 --> 19:45.080
[Mari] Karin!

216
19:45.998 --> 19:48.417
I think it's someone's birthday today!

217
19:48.501 --> 19:49.960
Mari. [chuckles]

218
19:51.295 --> 19:52.505
[sighs]

219
19:52.588 --> 19:54.340
Huh? What's wrong?

220
19:55.216 --> 19:56.342
What happened?

221
19:58.385 --> 20:00.387
-[Mari whining] -Well, it makes sense now,

222
20:00.471 --> 20:02.264
why you don't seem like yourself.

223
20:02.348 --> 20:05.059
He told me he's been drifting around without a care in the world

224
20:05.142 --> 20:07.353
and then when he came to Charo Island, he saw me,

225
20:07.436 --> 20:10.064
and that's what made him decide he should stay here.

226
20:10.147 --> 20:12.358
But we started dating and now he wants to leave,

227
20:12.441 --> 20:14.985
-so that must be the reason why, right? -Would you stop it?

228
20:15.069 --> 20:17.863
-We're talking about Kunam, right? -Mm-hmm.

229
20:19.281 --> 20:23.285
I'm worried about Karin. She seems pretty out of sorts.

230
20:24.370 --> 20:25.871
Yeah, I'm worried too.

231
20:25.955 --> 20:26.956
[Mari sighs]

232
20:27.540 --> 20:31.043
Splitting up, it's a really hard thing to go through.

233
20:33.087 --> 20:35.965
That's not gonna be a thing with us, right?

234
20:36.966 --> 20:39.051
You're going to stay here in Japan, aren't you?

235
20:44.723 --> 20:47.685
RESIDENCE CARD

236
20:47.768 --> 20:49.770
-[line ringing] -[footsteps pacing]

237
20:52.022 --> 20:53.023
[sighs]

238
20:53.732 --> 20:54.817
I called them too late.

239
20:55.526 --> 20:56.527
They're not answering.

240
20:56.610 --> 20:57.903
I can't believe you.

241
20:57.987 --> 21:00.114
This is why I told you to take care of it early.

242
21:00.197 --> 21:02.575
I guess I didn't realize how the time had flown.

243
21:04.285 --> 21:06.704
Someone will answer soon. Don't hang up yet.

244
21:06.787 --> 21:08.664
[call connects]

245
21:08.747 --> 21:11.709
-Oh. They picked up. -Okay, here we go.

246
21:13.878 --> 21:15.546
Uh, yes. Good afternoon.

247
21:15.629 --> 21:19.216
My working holiday visa is going to expire soon

248
21:19.717 --> 21:23.721
and I'm wondering what steps I need to take next to extend my residency.

249
21:23.804 --> 21:26.223
[public servant] Those visas aren't eligible to be extended.

250
21:26.807 --> 21:28.475
-Huh? -There's a given period

251
21:28.559 --> 21:31.061
in which you're supposed to request a change of status.

252
21:31.854 --> 21:33.522
If you don't apply for a standard work visa,

253
21:33.606 --> 21:35.608
you need to leave before yours expires.

254
21:35.691 --> 21:39.570
What? [stammers] You're saying I would be overstaying without it?

255
21:40.946 --> 21:42.489
"Overstay"?

256
21:42.573 --> 21:44.909
Does that mean I would get deported?

257
21:44.992 --> 21:46.952
They can't deport him…

258
21:48.203 --> 21:49.371
[Kunam] Understood. Thank you.

259
21:51.832 --> 21:53.709
What are we going to do?

260
22:00.132 --> 22:01.300
I'm sorry.

261
22:02.676 --> 22:04.178
I should get going.

262
22:09.475 --> 22:12.645
That was weird. What the heck was that?

263
22:12.728 --> 22:14.271
Sorry to do this out of the blue.

264
22:14.355 --> 22:15.981
Oh, no, I understand.

265
22:16.941 --> 22:17.942
Go on.

266
22:20.736 --> 22:24.239
Hey, you! I texted you all day yesterday, why'd you ignore me?

267
22:26.325 --> 22:29.078
I think that we should take a break.

268
22:30.663 --> 22:32.247
-What? -I need some space.

269
22:34.917 --> 22:36.168
It's for the best.

270
22:43.717 --> 22:45.594
[Mari, whining] His visa is expiring soon,

271
22:45.678 --> 22:48.806
and he doesn't wanna spend any of his time with me at all.

272
22:49.390 --> 22:51.809
This is why I was telling you I don't want

273
22:51.892 --> 22:54.728
-to get in a serious relationship! -Mari, Mari, Mari.

274
22:54.812 --> 22:58.607
I think Kunam is serious about you too. Something could've happened.

275
22:58.691 --> 23:00.859
-Mmm? -Mmm.

276
23:02.236 --> 23:05.114
-That's what I thought in the beginning… -Mm-hmm.

277
23:05.197 --> 23:06.991
[♪ quirky music playing]

278
23:09.743 --> 23:11.245
[♪ sensual music playing]

279
23:12.204 --> 23:14.206
[footsteps echoing]

280
23:33.267 --> 23:35.185
-[clerk 1 gasps] Oh, my gosh! -[clerk 2] Oh!

281
23:35.269 --> 23:37.438
-[clerk 1] You look so handsome. -[clerks clapping]

282
23:37.521 --> 23:39.314
Oh, this fits you perfectly.

283
23:39.398 --> 23:42.151
It looks great on you. Makes you look like a model.

284
23:42.234 --> 23:43.777
-Oh, thank you, ma'am. -[clerk 1] Uh-huh.

285
23:43.861 --> 23:46.030
[clerk 2] Are you shopping for a matchmaking date?

286
23:46.113 --> 23:47.281
[Mari gasps]

287
23:47.364 --> 23:50.200
-Oh, well, um… Something like that, yes. -[clerks exclaim]

288
23:50.284 --> 23:51.952
[clerk 2] I wonder what type of girl she is.

289
23:52.036 --> 23:53.287
[clerk 1] Oh, I'm jealous.

290
23:53.370 --> 23:54.955
Wait… Were you following him?

291
23:55.539 --> 23:57.499
No, no, it was a total coincidence.

292
23:57.583 --> 23:59.668
Mm-hmm. So then what?

293
23:59.752 --> 24:03.005
-I saw him meeting another woman. -He was with a girl?

294
24:03.088 --> 24:05.049
-Mm-hmm. -Huh?

295
24:05.132 --> 24:06.633
[♪ quirky music playing]

296
24:10.262 --> 24:11.263
[Kunam] Over here.

297
24:11.346 --> 24:14.058
-[chuckles] It's been forever. -I know, right?

298
24:15.934 --> 24:18.937
Sorry for calling out of nowhere. Thanks for coming.

299
24:19.021 --> 24:20.439
-Yeah. -[chuckles]

300
24:21.398 --> 24:22.858
So here it is…

301
24:24.318 --> 24:26.779
What? That's amazing! You can ask me anything.

302
24:26.862 --> 24:27.863
-Really? -Yeah.

303
24:27.946 --> 24:29.907
-Seriously, thank you. -No, of course.

304
24:29.990 --> 24:31.408
[both chuckle]

305
24:32.618 --> 24:34.244
[person] Give me a smile and just let it feel natural.

306
24:34.328 --> 24:35.329
NOW CALLING… KUNAM

307
24:35.412 --> 24:37.081
-I wanna see you do it. -I can do that.

308
24:38.207 --> 24:41.001
-[laughs] Yeah, that's totally perfect. -[phone buzzing]

309
24:45.047 --> 24:46.840
-Should we get going? -Yeah.

310
24:48.092 --> 24:49.927
-[Kunam] Let's do it. -Okay. Great.

311
24:54.389 --> 24:55.474
-Thanks. -[Kunam] Mmm.

312
24:57.684 --> 24:58.685
[sighs]

313
24:59.436 --> 25:01.814
Was this all just so he could get away from me?

314
25:05.317 --> 25:06.360
[Karin sighs]

315
25:07.027 --> 25:08.445
I guess I should go.

316
25:18.372 --> 25:19.790
No, stay as long as you want.

317
25:24.503 --> 25:25.504
Mari.

318
25:27.422 --> 25:28.423
Cheer up, okay?

319
25:28.507 --> 25:29.508
Mm-hmm.

320
25:32.136 --> 25:33.846
I want you to cheer up too.

321
25:34.763 --> 25:35.764
Hmm?

322
25:36.849 --> 25:37.850
Well…

323
25:40.644 --> 25:42.896
What I mean is that Yubin, as far as I could tell,

324
25:42.980 --> 25:45.315
was really serious about you too.

325
25:48.152 --> 25:50.487
I know 'cause I heard it for myself.

326
25:51.071 --> 25:52.239
[Kunam screaming]

327
25:52.865 --> 25:54.158
[in Korean] Darn it!

328
25:54.241 --> 25:56.869
Ugh, I'm sick of bugs.

329
25:56.952 --> 25:57.953
Ugh.

330
25:58.036 --> 26:00.247
This field work is seriously no joke.

331
26:01.123 --> 26:04.501
I mean, Karin is already so frail, so why does she have to farm the hard way?

332
26:04.585 --> 26:06.587
Why can't she just use a greenhouse and do it the easier way?

333
26:06.670 --> 26:07.754
[Yubin] What?

334
26:07.838 --> 26:09.882
The easier way?

335
26:10.924 --> 26:14.219
Fruits are meant to grow with the rhythm of the seasons.

336
26:14.303 --> 26:16.513
They hold the flavor of the season.

337
26:16.597 --> 26:20.100
They're meant to take effort.

338
26:20.184 --> 26:21.935
Here, take a look.

339
26:22.019 --> 26:24.354
Look at this majestic nature.

340
26:24.438 --> 26:27.941
I want to know how delicious strawberries would turn out

341
26:28.025 --> 26:30.569
when they are grown in nature.

342
26:36.283 --> 26:37.534
[in English] He really said all of that?

343
26:37.618 --> 26:38.869
Mmm.

344
26:41.955 --> 26:43.415
Okay, I'm gonna go.

345
26:43.498 --> 26:44.541
Hmm.

346
26:55.135 --> 26:56.261
[grunts]

347
26:59.431 --> 27:01.558
-Oh, hi. -Hello, Karin.

348
27:02.184 --> 27:03.727
I just need a signature from you, please.

349
27:03.810 --> 27:05.729
Yep, no problem. Thank you.

350
27:05.812 --> 27:07.481
-Here. If you don't mind. -Okay, great.

351
27:07.564 --> 27:11.568
SENT FROM: AKATSUKI CITY, FUKUOKA

352
27:12.402 --> 27:13.403
-Here. -All set.

353
27:13.487 --> 27:15.072
Your copy will be on the package.

354
27:17.074 --> 27:19.493
-Here you go. Have a good day. -Yes. Thanks so much.

355
27:31.088 --> 27:32.130
[phone buzzes]

356
27:36.969 --> 27:41.056
YOUR PACKAGE HAS BEEN DELIVERED

357
27:45.310 --> 27:46.687
Ah… [sighs]

358
28:23.306 --> 28:27.477
DEAR KARIN

359
28:30.731 --> 28:31.815
[♪ tender piano music playing]

360
28:49.374 --> 28:50.667
[Yubin, in Korean] Dear Karin.

361
29:00.886 --> 29:01.887
-[in English] A hot coffee? -Yeah.

362
29:01.970 --> 29:03.430
Sure thing, coming right up.

363
29:16.068 --> 29:17.069
[in Korean] What's this?

364
29:22.783 --> 29:24.284
Birthday?

365
29:28.538 --> 29:30.373
Happy birthday.

366
29:32.542 --> 29:35.545
This is the first letter I write to you, Karin.

367
29:37.714 --> 29:39.549
I could say these words in person…

368
29:40.550 --> 29:43.261
But I'm writing them down in a letter

369
29:44.262 --> 29:46.223
in hopes that it will help convey my sincerity.

370
29:47.891 --> 29:51.269
My Japanese isn't all that good,

371
29:51.353 --> 29:53.271
but I hope it comes through.

372
29:57.609 --> 30:01.905
There's something important I have to tell you.

373
30:03.573 --> 30:06.451
I should have told you much sooner.

374
30:06.535 --> 30:08.995
I'm sorry I waited so long.

375
30:11.331 --> 30:14.960
We didn't run into each other by chance.

376
30:15.836 --> 30:18.255
In order to sell off my property on that island,

377
30:19.005 --> 30:22.217
I needed to get ahold of yours. I was here…

378
30:22.300 --> 30:23.844
[in English] You ruined my farm, didn't you?

379
30:23.927 --> 30:27.597
[Yubin, in Korean] …to win you over so I could get the land.

380
30:29.808 --> 30:32.435
That's why I got close to you.

381
30:34.146 --> 30:35.438
But now…

382
30:36.940 --> 30:37.941
I couldn't care less about it.

383
30:39.484 --> 30:43.196
Because now, this place has become important to me.

384
30:43.280 --> 30:45.532
[Karin, Yubin laughing]

385
30:47.576 --> 30:51.079
[Yubin] And the people who have accepted me.

386
30:51.163 --> 30:52.205
[villagers chattering]

387
30:53.039 --> 30:54.624
[Yubin, in Korean] And you too, Karin.

388
30:56.459 --> 30:59.129
I thought I was helping you out,

389
31:00.463 --> 31:03.049
but you were the one helping me.

390
31:10.307 --> 31:13.101
-I love the breakfasts we have together… -[Karin] Chopsticks go in the front.

391
31:13.185 --> 31:15.645
-…with our chopsticks placed differently. -[both] Thanks for the meal.

392
31:17.230 --> 31:21.860
I love driving around on your truck, feeling the breeze on this island.

393
31:23.695 --> 31:26.198
And the night you leaned on my shoulder…

394
31:28.241 --> 31:30.869
It felt as if a star had fallen right before me.

395
31:31.870 --> 31:33.914
Before I knew it, I was…

396
31:35.290 --> 31:38.001
wishing upon that star to stay with you.

397
31:41.087 --> 31:44.299
To spend these ordinary yet extraordinary days with you…

398
31:45.217 --> 31:48.094
And stay by your side forever and ever.

399
31:48.178 --> 31:49.721
-Love. -Love.

400
31:50.931 --> 31:53.433
If it means that you'll get to shine bright…

401
31:55.185 --> 31:58.396
I'm willing to remain in the dark of the night.

402
31:59.940 --> 32:01.775
That's how much I pray for you to be happy.

403
32:06.655 --> 32:07.656
Karin.

404
32:08.949 --> 32:09.991
I like you.

405
32:11.201 --> 32:12.285
I care about you deeply.

406
32:13.036 --> 32:14.371
[Karin sniffles]

407
32:14.454 --> 32:17.582
With love and respect, Yubin.

408
32:21.419 --> 32:22.420
[sniffles]

409
33:25.358 --> 33:26.401
[cries]

410
33:32.907 --> 33:33.908
[sniffles]

411
33:38.246 --> 33:40.165
[sobbing]

412
34:03.897 --> 34:04.898
[chuckles softly]

413
34:07.859 --> 34:08.860
[sobs]

414
34:15.408 --> 34:16.993
[♪ music fades out]

415
34:32.384 --> 34:33.468
Yubin!

416
34:34.010 --> 34:35.136
Yubin…

417
34:40.433 --> 34:44.521
DOWNTOWN REDEVELOPMENT PROJECT

418
34:46.439 --> 34:48.024
-[sighs] -[door opens]

419
34:48.108 --> 34:50.443
-[director] Good work, everyone. -Oh…

420
34:52.570 --> 34:53.780
Hello, sir.

421
34:55.365 --> 34:59.536
When is the deadline for this model?

422
34:59.619 --> 35:01.830
In a month and a half.

423
35:01.913 --> 35:03.790
We don't have much time.

424
35:04.457 --> 35:06.209
Here's how we approach this.

425
35:06.292 --> 35:08.211
-A complete overhaul. -[snaps fingers]

426
35:08.294 --> 35:10.505
-Keep it premium. -[employee gasps]

427
35:10.588 --> 35:13.341
Sounds like a tagline.

428
35:13.425 --> 35:15.260
[laughing]

429
35:18.763 --> 35:19.889
Mr. Lee?

430
35:20.640 --> 35:22.058
Please begin.

431
35:22.142 --> 35:24.185
URBAN REGENERATION THAT PRESERVES MEMORIES

432
35:24.269 --> 35:27.731
I'm the director in charge of this project, Lee Yubin.

433
35:29.023 --> 35:32.736
I'd like to propose a completely new angle

434
35:32.819 --> 35:35.196
that's different from anything we've done before.

435
35:35.280 --> 35:37.532
The market is the identity of the neighborhood

436
35:37.615 --> 35:41.244
that has accumulated the memories of the locals' lives.

437
35:41.828 --> 35:46.958
I believe preserving the said identity is the essence of this project.

438
35:48.668 --> 35:49.753
We will selectively…

439
35:49.836 --> 35:51.671
That doesn't sound like him.

440
35:51.755 --> 35:56.259
He's known to get rid of anything that misaligns with his aesthetic.

441
35:56.342 --> 35:58.094
[Yubin] The history and unique charm…

442
35:58.178 --> 35:59.429
[director] Mr. Lee.

443
36:00.096 --> 36:05.602
We heard about your groundbreaking talent.

444
36:06.978 --> 36:08.563
This is disappointing.

445
36:09.147 --> 36:11.900
What people seek from the redevelopment

446
36:11.983 --> 36:17.572
is a clean, new living space, not some old market.

447
36:17.655 --> 36:18.782
[Yubin] This redevelopment plan…

448
36:19.783 --> 36:23.953
is more than a simple business initiative.

449
36:24.037 --> 36:25.872
It's about the identity of the neighborhood…

450
36:25.955 --> 36:31.878
How's identity going to make us money? Does it bring in advertisers?

451
36:33.296 --> 36:37.926
You're with Bella Terra, not Y:SPACE.

452
36:38.760 --> 36:41.262
I can't believe your company lasted as long as it did.

453
36:44.182 --> 36:45.308
[director scoffs]

454
36:45.391 --> 36:47.268
Show the schedule.

455
36:49.479 --> 36:53.691
We're clearing out everything, including the traditional market.

456
36:54.317 --> 36:58.822
I want a report on the revised plan by the end of the week.

457
37:05.745 --> 37:08.915
[♪ melancholic music playing]

458
37:40.947 --> 37:42.949
[♪ melancholic music continues]

459
38:13.187 --> 38:14.188
[♪ music ends]

460
38:20.111 --> 38:21.404
[sighs]

461
38:30.246 --> 38:32.248
[♪ emotional music playing]

462
38:37.837 --> 38:39.797
[Karin, in English] It's important to have your own special spot.

463
38:39.881 --> 38:43.426
Some place all to yourself when you're feeling overwhelmed.

464
38:43.509 --> 38:44.969
Do you have somewhere like that?

465
38:45.053 --> 38:46.054
[in Korean] Yes.

466
38:47.764 --> 38:48.765
For me…

467
38:50.642 --> 38:51.768
This place.

468
38:51.851 --> 38:53.686
[in English] Wow… That's nice.

469
38:53.770 --> 38:55.229
-[in Korean] Isn't it pretty? -[in English] Cool.

470
38:55.939 --> 38:59.901
[in Korean] This is where I go when things get really tough.

471
39:01.235 --> 39:03.279
If you ever come to Seoul, I'll take you there.

472
39:04.322 --> 39:06.407
[in English] Hmm. Sounds good to me.

473
39:08.326 --> 39:12.038
KARIN

474
39:12.121 --> 39:14.123
[♪ music continues]

475
39:22.590 --> 39:23.758
[sighs]

476
39:29.973 --> 39:33.017
[phone buzzing]

477
39:43.903 --> 39:45.279
[buzzing continues]

478
39:52.328 --> 39:53.329
[in Korean] Hello?

479
39:55.581 --> 39:56.582
[Karin, in English] Hello?

480
40:14.642 --> 40:15.768
[stammers]

481
40:17.645 --> 40:19.230
[♪ romantic song playing]

482
40:28.114 --> 40:29.115
[in Korean] Karin.

483
40:30.825 --> 40:32.410
How did you…

484
40:36.164 --> 40:37.165
[in English] Yubin…

485
40:39.709 --> 40:40.710
[sighs]

486
40:43.755 --> 40:44.964
[in Korean] How have you been?

487
40:45.590 --> 40:47.550
[breathing heavily]

488
40:49.886 --> 40:51.512
Are you feeling okay?

489
40:52.472 --> 40:53.890
Did you get sick at all?

490
40:56.059 --> 41:00.063
[sighs] I should have told you sooner.

491
41:03.274 --> 41:06.527
I'm sorry, I… I'm really sorry.

492
41:08.362 --> 41:09.572
[in English] I read it.

493
41:13.993 --> 41:15.078
Your letter…

494
41:24.796 --> 41:26.464
[breathes shakily, whimpers]

495
42:04.794 --> 42:06.337
[Yubin, in Korean] I wanted to see you.

496
42:09.215 --> 42:10.675
[Karin, in English] I missed you so much.

497
42:59.223 --> 43:00.516
MERRY BERRY LOVE

498
43:00.600 --> 43:01.601
NEXT EPISODE

499
43:01.684 --> 43:03.311
[Yubin, in English] In Korean, it's gamja.

500
43:03.394 --> 43:04.645
[Karin] I've always wanted to try it.

501
43:05.271 --> 43:06.272
[in Korean] With a boyfriend…

502
43:06.981 --> 43:08.983
[in English] I wish I could stay here with you forever,

503
43:09.066 --> 43:11.110
but I have to go back to Japan…
